From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:33:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Let XPath see through entity references, as Windows
 does.

What an entity reference holds takes its place on every axis: MSXML 6 looks
through all references, MSXML 3 through those not in another one, leaving
out the references in them and all they hold.  MSXML 6 selects nothing
from a reference, MSXML 3 with XPath nothing it holds.  An XSL pattern has
a node for the DTD, XPath none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/selection.c b/dlls/msxml3/selection.c
index 9e745e0cce4..2cb043ab40a 100644
--- a/dlls/msxml3/selection.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/selection.c
@@ -602,6 +602,10 @@ static HRESULT select_nodes(struct domnode *node, const WCHAR *query, bool xpath
     struct xpath_context *ctxt;
     HRESULT hr;
 
+    /* XPath sees through entity references: MSXML 6 selects nothing from one (Windows 11) */
+    if (node->type == NODE_ENTITY_REFERENCE && node->owner && domdoc_version(node->owner) >= MSXML6)
+        return E_FAIL;
+
     ctxt = xpath_create_context(xpath, node);
 
     result = xpath_eval(query, ctxt);
